bol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A random pseudograph with these degrees, by the configuration model: vertex i gets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"degreeSequence[i]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" stubs, the stubs are shuffled, and the k-th stub of the first half is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paired with the k-th of the second half. Every pairing of the stubs is equally likely, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loops and parallel edges occur; a self-loop counts 2 toward its vertex’s degree, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every vertex has exactly its degree. The edges are at positions "},{"code":"0..<m","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in pairing order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each written (first-half end, second-half end). The shuffle is Fisher–Yates, i from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last stub down to 1 swapped with "},{"code":"below(i + 1)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/randomgraphs\/multigraphs\/pseudograph\/configurationmodel(degreesequence:using:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/RandomGraphs\/documentation\/RandomGraphs\/Multigraphs\/Pseudograph\/configurationModel(degreeSequence:using:)"},"doc://RandomGraphs/documentation/RandomGraphs/Multigraphs/Pseudograph/configurationModel(degreeSequence:)":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/randomgraphs\/multigraphs\/pseudograph\/configurationmodel(degreesequence:)","type":"topic","title":"configurationModel(degreeSequence:)","abstract":[{"code":"configurationModel(degreeSequence:using:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with the system’s random number generator."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"configurationModel"},{"kind":"te